+- AC-1: Parsing, one exact rule. The rule matches how compose `env_file: format: raw` delivers the value to the api service. Docker Compose 5.6.0, the version on t2-dev and, read-only, on the production host, was probed with fake values: lines starting with `#` are comments; leading whitespace before the key is dropped; the line is split on the first `=`; the value is taken verbatim: quotes are kept as characters, trailing spaces are kept, and a `#` inside the value is kept; a final CR is stripped; the last duplicate wins; a key holding whitespace (including an `export KEY=` line) makes compose refuse the whole file. derive takes the value exactly as compose would give it, except that it is stricter. It refuses, with a fixed REASON: no GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY line; more than one such line; an `export` form; an empty value; any CR, LF, NUL or other control character (tab included) in the value. Verify by: pytest `test_derive_parse_*` with fake values, one per case: plain, base64 containing `=`, double-quoted, single-quoted, trailing spaces, CRLF line, `export` line, duplicate, missing, empty and tab. Plus a parity test that runs the real `docker compose config` on the same fake env file and asserts that derive's value equals compose's value for every accepted case. Source: inferred: from ticket:GoodQA goodqa#16148 -- the lead's ruling 1 (Sonnet 1, Opus S8), relayed 2026-11-16
+- AC-2: Derivation and ownership. The directory /etc/goodqa/job-secrets is root:root 0711. The file is root:goodqa-jobsecret 0440. goodqa-jobsecret is a dedicated group with the fixed gid 64910, and no host account is a member. derive creates the group if it is absent (`groupadd -r -g 64910`). It refuses if: gid 64910 has another name or any member; the name has another gid; the directory or file exists with a different owner, mode or type. derive writes the value byte for byte, without decoding. The worker's decodePrivateKey (apps/intelligence-worker/src/github.ts:51) accepts raw or base64 PEM. The write steps, never resolving a path twice: Open the directory O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW. Create a random temp name with O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW relative to that directory fd. fchown and fchmod on the file fd, write, fsync. Rename within the directory fd. fsync the directory. An unchanged value leaves the file untouched. The comparison opens the old file O_NOFOLLOW and compares in memory; nothing is printed. The only output is one line, `job secret github-app-private-key: written|unchanged|REFUSED REASON`, with REASON a fixed phrase. Verify by: pytest with a fake root, run in a throwaway user namespace or container on t2-dev: owner, group, modes and byte equality; idempotency: mtime unchanged on a second run; no temp file left after a kill between write and rename; a symlink planted mid-run by a non-root directory owner, through a hook between create and rename, never makes root touch a path outside the directory, and derive refuses; a uid or gid collision (gid 64910 taken by another name, the group with a member, the name with another gid) is refused with nothing written. Source: inferred: from ticket:GoodQA goodqa#16148 -- the lead's ruling 2 (Opus S1, Sonnet 2), relayed 2026-11-16
+- AC-3: Mount and group. Only job-dispatcher mounts /etc/goodqa/job-secrets, read-only, at /run/goodqa-secrets, and only job-dispatcher has `group_add: ["64910"]`. The create-guard still refuses any job-container bind or mount, including one of /etc/goodqa/job-secrets or /run/goodqa-secrets. Verify by: real `docker compose config`: the bind and group_add appear on job-dispatcher only, with `read_only: true`; create-guard vitest cases: a create body with HostConfig.Binds `/etc/goodqa/job-secrets:/s:ro`, and one with Mounts of type bind for /run/goodqa-secrets. Each is refused with 403. Source: inferred: from ticket:GoodQA goodqa#16148 -- the lead's ruling 6 (Sonnet 3)
+- AC-4: Injection. A dispatcher env key `JOB_ENVFILE_KIND__VAR=PATH` supplies VAR to that kind's job env. It is read at each launch. It is honoured only if `KIND__VAR` is in the dispatcher's compiled allow-list, today only `INTELLIGENCE_WORKER__GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`. A JOB_ENV_KIND__VAR whose VAR ends in `_FILE` keeps its literal meaning, unchanged. The read: Reject PATH unless it is absolute, has no `..` segment, and its parent is exactly /run/goodqa-secrets. open O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW. fstat the same fd: it must be a regular file. Read at most 64 KiB plus 1 byte from that fd and refuse if more arrives. Remove one trailing LF. Other kinds are unaffected. Verify by: vitest on buildServer with a temp secrets dir and a stub docker. The env-file passed for intelligence-worker carries VAR, and no other kind's does. A non-allow-listed JOB_ENVFILE key is ignored and logged by name. Source: inferred: from ticket:GoodQA goodqa#16148 -- the existing JOB_ENV mechanism, extended under the lead's ruling 9 (Opus S5, S6)
